WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.020
The apocalypse is here, ladies and gentlemen, and so is 
my breakdown of "American Horror Story: Apocalypse".

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.020
Sorry it's taken a few days to get this out,

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.860
but I was busy finishing 
my "Castle Rock Explained" series.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:12.060
But enough about that.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.220
We're here for the end of the world, so let's get into it.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:20.880
Socialite Coco St. Pierre Vanderbilt is getting 
her hair done by famous hairstylist, Mr. Gallant,

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.100
or as the French say, "Gall-oh".

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.060
In fact, she even says 
he could be the next Chris McMillan,

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:31.900
which, for those of you who aren't on the Rodeo Drive socialite scene, is a famous real-life Hollywood stylist.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.600
Also, huge points for the makeup artist
 who even put glitter on Evan Peters' fingernails.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.920
Mallory, played here by 
Billie Lourd, Carrie Fisher's daughter,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:45.960
is Coco's assistant who really wants Coco to have her finely pressed juice because they're so in right now.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.820
But then something even 
worse than a bad haircut happens:

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.480
A ballistic missile is inbound for L.A.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:56.180
Coco's billionaire father calls and 
informs her he has four spots reserved for the family

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.080
in the event of a nuclear fallout.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.980
But because he's in Hong Kong, 
he and the fam won't make it.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:05.560
The signal goes out after what can only be 
assumed is a nuclear bomb hitting the city.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.780
Coco's boyfriend, played here by 
"Billy on the Street", is at work,

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.040
busy preparing a six-part limited series of "Free Willy".

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.920
Numerous international strikes have been confirmed 
and Coco tells him to meet her at the airport.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.820
Mr. Gallant comes to get his Nana Evie, 
a widow of a former MGM studio owner.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.760
She tells him it's all fake news,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.100
"You are fake news."

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.020
and that she'll bring the burnt champagne,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.800
which for you non-millionaire 
widows of major Hollywood studios means

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:36.300
a bottle of champagne that was frozen 
at one point and lost some of its prestige.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:38.220
Kind of like Nana Evie herself.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:43.420
Coco says she'll give Mallory her brother's tickets and she needs her assistant. She's helpless without her.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.620
And Mallory completely 
ditches her family and agrees to go.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.180
These dudes have apparently decided 
it's a great time to steal some fruit,

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.060
before somebody's body comes crashing onto the car.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.840
Team Coco arrives at the airport,

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.680
and I love how these dudes 
are casually just doing their jobs,

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.080
even though the world is ending. That's commitment.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:04.900
The driver here has some sweet "Mad Max" 
gloves, and I gotta say, he's pretty badass.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.340
Mr. Gallant rolls up with 
Nana Evie and begs her to let them on.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.000
After all, who's gonna do her hair when the world ends?

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.360
The airport workers then decide 
to turn on them, coming for the plane.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:19.200
Jason Statham over here fights them off as Coco releases Brock from his monogamy arrangement

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.340
and they escape from the ravaging horde.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.860
And can we all just have a moment of silence 
for this woman who tried to steal some meat?

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:29.220
Brock sees Coco's plane fly overhead as 
he leaves her with some parting words of love -

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:30.620
"YOU BITCH!"

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:34.560
I wouldn't be surprised if we see this 
character make a return later on in the series.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:40.020
In the plane, Mallory checks to see where they're going, but the pilots are gone - and even worse, the stewardess.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:45.040
A bomb blast goes off, and for a brief moment, 
you can see the plane automatically adjust,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.520
suggesting it's an automatic plane 
or mysterious force controlling it.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.400
Flashback 40 minutes before the bomb,

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:55.520
and we're introduced to Timmy, 
who's eagerly awaiting his results from UCLA.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.760
And he gets in! Way to go, Timmy!

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.340
And did you catch "American Horror Story" 
Easter egg of Pepper being one of the male recipients?

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.160
Then dad comes in, being a total 
buzzkill, explaining it's World War III.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.820
But before they can think of a plan,
two agents from the Cooperative storm in,

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:16.000
explaining that Timothy has been selected to 
survive because of his exceptional genetic makeup.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.020
This video has been sponsored by AncestryDNA.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:22.900
He refuses to go when he's forcefully taken by 
super soldiers and locked in an underground bunker.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.540
There, he meets Emily, before the bomb goes off.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.740
Apparently, his super genetics 
make him susceptible to crying.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.600
Two weeks later, they're taken to Outpost 3,

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.960
one of ten around the world, 
built in minimal fallout zones.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.080
Which is a bit odd, since if they 
were built in minimal fallout zones,

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.740
they would a) either have known 
where the bombs were to hit beforehand,

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.120
or b) built them really, really fast.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.180
Which we'll find out later they didn't.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:54.160
Timmy and Emily are given hazmat suits and dropped off before being greeted by the welcoming committee.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.440
Kylo Ren leads them across a field where 
they see two people dressed in Amish clothing,

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:01.740
pleading that they won't do it again before being shot.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.780
The masks these guys wear are eerily similar to the plague doctor masks from medieval times.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:11.380
The extended noses were used to
 stuff herbes and spices to ward off miasma,

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.680
the belief that disease was spread through the air.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.720
Down in the bunker, they're decontaminated,

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.180
and we catch a brief glimpse
of Kathy Bates's character Mead,

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.060
who we'll later learn is the 
head of security for the bunker.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:26.980
Sarah Paulson arrives, playing Wilhelmina 
Venable, and welcomes them to Outpost 3.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.500
Her last name sounding a lot like venerable,

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.180
which is a common epithet used in Christian theology

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:37.280
to denote someone who should be given respect 
based on their age, character or wisdom.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:41.040
She says the bomb was a cleansing fire
 and that this is a new beginning.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.719
The Cooperative, the organization 
in charge of putting this all together,

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.740
is a collection of the dozen 
greatest minds mankind has to offer.

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.980
The twelve are known as "the Visionaries",

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.560
and my guess is we'll get to 
meet some of them later on.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.460
There aren't any generators down here,
 but there is some form of electricity,

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:00.620
considering the keycard used to get in and the elevator.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:04.360
Timmy and Emily are told they're 
"Purples" and assigned their own suites.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.600
Purples are elite, the worthy, chosen to survive.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.640
Unlike the Greys, who are the worker ants.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:14.800
And the Outpost itself is even designed like 
an anthill with multiple winding pathways.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:18.960
Emily asks what Wilhelmina's role
 is in all of this, to which she responds

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.800
She's the strong right arm of the 
Cooperative, and down here, there are rules.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.000
They aren't allowed to leave due to 
the risk of "canker puss monsters".

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.580
And worst of all, no unauthorised copulation of any kind,

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.640
which was what these two were apparently doing.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.500
Timmy takes a shower when 
he sees "666" in the condensation.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.960
A voice whispers, "Beware, Timothy".

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:43.800
Now, this is a huge loose thread, because we don't 
come back to either of these by the end of the episode.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:48.180
In time for cocktails, it looks like 
they're wearing attire from the 1800s South,

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.820
which leads me to believe 
they're somewhere in Louisiana,

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.240
which would tie into season three's "Coven".

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:57.360
Mr. Gallant complains about the 
same song being played every night,

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.900
"Calling Occupants of Interplanetary Craft" 
by The Carpenters,

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.900
a song about telepathy 
and reaching out to other worlds.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.940
Mallory has been relegated to a Grey

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:09.180
and pleads to Coco for her to go 
to Venable and make her a Purple.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.620
Venable rings a bell, indicating 
their delicious cube dinners are ready.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:16.880
Each cube containing every vitamin 
they need, and Coco ain't havin' it.

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:19.340
She wants real food, like "Pirate's Booty".

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:23.080
Venable puts her in her place 
and explains the gravity of the situation:

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.980
They only have 18 months of nutrition stocked,

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:29.040
and if they want to survive, they need to ration carefully.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.820
Not to mention there's been a 
perimeter alert. Something penetrated the ground.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:35.700
A carrier pigeon with a message from their benefactors:

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:38.660
Three out of the ten Outposts have been overrun.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:42.720
They're the last of humanity, 
the last vestiges of civilized life.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.560
Mead is informed by Mrs. Lurch that there's a 
spike in contamination coming from the room.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.620
Someone has broken the clean rule.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:55.540
The Geiger counter, a machine used to detect 
radiation, identifies the culprits: Mr. Gallant and Stu.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:00.080
They're sent to the decontamination showers, 
where Stu is shot because his levels are too high.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.860
At night, Ms. Venable and Mead hold a secret meeting,

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.920
where they break their 
own rules by wearing purple outfits.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.960
Venable says they're the only ones
 that matter, and we learn Stu was set up:

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.720
Mead put the counter to a higher sensitivity.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:15.920
This was either to keep them 
in control or to thin the herd.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:21.760
They play an old 1940's Whitman set of Old Maid,
a Victorian card game for two or more players,

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:26.580
probably deriving from an ancient gambling game 
in which the loser pays for the drinks.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.340
The drinks here being mineral water.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.900
They both relish the pain they caused their captives,

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:34.500
and how they're undermining the 
Cooperative by making up their own rules.

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:37.540
Venable says there is no Cooperative, it's only them.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.480
Which doesn't necessarily mean 
the Cooperative doesn't exist,

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.260
it just means they've gone rogue.

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:45.940
The others are still getting over
the death of Stu when Venable arrives.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:50.160
As a consolation, she's prepared a
Bonne Bouche, a French word for "treat".

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.480
Another hint this could be taking place in the South.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.900
Apparently, they have "resources" for special occasions.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:01.600
Venable uses this occasion to stress how 
it's important to follow the rules for everyone's safety.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:07.600
Gallant takes out what looks like a tooth before everyone realizes that the stew they're eating is, well, Stu.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.620
"The stew is Stu!"

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.600
The group argues whether 
or not the food was actually Stu,

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:15.800
when the radio changes to 
Maureen McGovern's "Morning After",

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:19.120
believing the Cooperative is saying, 
"Hang on, we're coming for you."

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:23.500
That is until 18 months pass, and if you 
recall, that's how long their supplies would last.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:26.500
No one has come and nuclear winter has taken over.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:31.160
Timmy and Emily are together, stating that 
even in all this death, something was born,

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:36.000
which could mean they broke a rule and a 
baby's on the way, or simply that their love was born.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:40.920
Venable cuts back supplies, stating they'll 
need to go to half a cube a day if they want to survive.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.785
Mutiny kicks in with Mallory stating, 
"I say we take our chances outside".

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.520
Since when do they let a Grey talk?

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:49.300
Mr. Gallant is about to be put in his place by Ms. Lurch,

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.180
when the alarm goes off, indicating a perimeter breach.

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:56.460
A horse-drawn carriage arrives, with a 
member of the Cooperative, Michael Langdon.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:00.560
And you know this guy means business 
because his badge says "unlimited clearance".

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.040
But look here at the signature for 
"President of the Cooperative".

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:08.460
It looks eerily like the word "Lucifer", 
and his ID number ends in 666.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:12.260
The same number found in Timmy's 
shower and the number of the Devil.

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.620
Inside, we get our first look of Michael Langdon,

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:17.500
who looks like he just came off 
the set of "Interview with a Vampire",

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:21.760
which, coincidentally enough, is also partly set in Louisiana.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.460
Mead kills one of the horses because it's contaminated,

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:28.000
and we get our first brief glimpse 
of what could be the puss monsters,

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.540
taking its corpse into the woods to be eaten.

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:34.940
Back in the bunker, Langdon tells Venable
that three more Outposts have been overrun

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.180
and three won't make it until the end of the year,

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:40.180
leaving their Outpost as the only one left,

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:41.820
but he's here to change that.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:46.380
There's another facility, an impregnable 
sanctuary with enough food for a decade,

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:49.300
but it's reserved only for those worthy of survival.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:53.900
He's here to weed out the worthy, which 
could mean next episode could be a bloodbath.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.700
I hope you'll stay tuned with me for more 
AHS breakdowns, and remember until next time:

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.700
Daddy loves you very much.

